[35.913089, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe evidence confirming that the \u001b[1;36;40mreport-worker\u001b[0m pod was killed due to exceeding its memory limit     \r\r\n(\u001b[1;36;40mOOMKilled\u001b[0m) rather than crashing on its own is as follows:                                          \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1;35mPod Description\u001b[0m                                                                                     \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[36m 1 \u001b[0m\u001b[1mState\u001b[0m:                                                                                           \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mThe container's \u001b[1mLast State\u001b[0m explicitly lists \u001b[1;36;40mReason: OOMKilled\u001b[0m.                                \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mExit Code: \u001b[1;36;40m137\u001b[0m, which is the standard code for termination due to memory exhaustion.          \r\r\n\u001b[36m 2 \u001b[0m\u001b[1mEvents\u001b[0m:                                                                                          \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mThe pod has repeated \u001b[1;36;40mBackOff\u001b[0m events indicating the container is failing to restart after being\r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mkilled.                                                                                       \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1;35mCommand Analysis\u001b[0m                                                                                    \r\r\n\r\r\nThe pod's command (\u001b[1;36;40mdd if=/dev/zero of=/dev/null bs=100M count=1\u001b[0m) is a memory-intensive operation.   \r\r\nThis aligns with the termination reason (\u001b[1;36;40mOOMKilled\u001b[0m), as the operation likely consumed more memory   \r\r\nthan the configured limit of 64Mi.                                                                  \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1;35mAbsence of Other Failure Indicators\u001b[0m                                                                 \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mThere are no indications of other failure reasons (e.g., syntax errors, missing dependencies) in \r\r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mthe pod description or events.                                                                   \r\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mThe termination reason is consistently \u001b[1;36;40mOOMKilled\u001b[0m, not \u001b[1;36;40mError\u001b[0m or other                             "]
[35.93467, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2KThe evidence confirming that the \u001b[1;36;40mreport-worker\u001b[0m pod was killed due to exceeding its memory limit     \r\r\n(\u001b[1;36;40mOOMKilled\u001b[0m) rather than crashing on its own is as follows:                                          \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1;35mPod Description\u001b[0m                                                                                     \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[36m 1 \u001b[0m\u001b[1mState\u001b[0m:                                                                                           \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mThe container's \u001b[1mLast State\u001b[0m explicitly lists \u001b[1;36;40mReason: OOMKilled\u001b[0m.                                \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mExit Code: \u001b[1;36;40m137\u001b[0m, which is the standard code for termination due to memory exhaustion.          \r\r\n\u001b[36m 2 \u001b[0m\u001b[1mEvents\u001b[0m:                                                                                          \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mThe pod has repeated \u001b[1;36;40mBackOff\u001b[0m events indicating the container is failing to restart after being\r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mkilled.                                                                                       \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1;35mCommand Analysis\u001b[0m                                                                                    \r\r\n\r\r\nThe pod's command (\u001b[1;36;40mdd if=/dev/zero of=/dev/null bs=100M count=1\u001b[0m) is a memory-intensive operation.   \r\r\nThis aligns with the termination reason (\u001b[1;36;40mOOMKilled\u001b[0m), as the operation likely consumed more memory   \r\r\nthan the configured limit of 64Mi.                                                                  \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1;35mAbsence of Other Failure Indicators\u001b[0m                                                                 \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mThere are no indications of other failure reasons (e.g., syntax errors, missing dependencies) in \r\r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mthe pod description or events.                                                                   \r\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mThe termination reason is consistently \u001b[1;36;40mOOMKilled\u001b[0m, not \u001b[1;36;40mError\u001b[0m or other crash-related reasons.      \r\r\n\r\r\nThis evidence strongly supports that the pod was killed due to memory exhaustion rather than        \r\r\ncrashing on its own. Let me know if you'd like further analysis or a specific fix applied.          \r\r\n\u001b[?25h"]
