[53.931425, "o", "\r\u001b[2KTo determine an appropriate memory limit for the \u001b[1;36;40mreport-worker\u001b[0m pod, we need to account for the      \r\r\nmemory-intensive nature of its command (\u001b[1;36;40mdd if=/dev/zero of=/dev/null bs=100M count=1\u001b[0m) and provide a \r\r\nbuffer to prevent further OOMKilled events.                                                         \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1;35mBasis for Recommendation\u001b[0m                                                                            \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[36m 1 \u001b[0m\u001b[1mCommand Behavior\u001b[0m:                                                                                \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mThe \u001b[1;36;40mdd\u001b[0m command with \u001b[1;36;40mbs=100M count=1\u001b[0m processes 100Mi of data in a single operation. This       \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m   \u001b[0msuggests the pod needs at least 100Mi of memory for the operation itself.                     \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mAdditional memory is required for the container runtime overhead and other system processes.  \r\r\n\u001b[36m 2 \u001b[0m\u001b[1mCurrent Limit\u001b[0m:                                                                                   \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mThe current memory limit is 64Mi, which is insufficient for the workload.                     \r\r\n\u001b[36m 3 \u001b[0m\u001b[1mBuffer for Stability\u001b[0m:                                                                            \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mTo ensure stability and avoid future OOMKilled events, a buffer of 50–100% above the estimated\r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mworkload memory usage is recommended.                                                         \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1;35mSuggested Memory Limit\u001b[0m                                                                              \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1mLimit\u001b[0m: 256Mi                                                                                     \r\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1mRequest\u001b[0m: 128Mi                                                                                   \r\r\n\r\r\nThis configuration provides ample room for                                                          "]
[53.955178, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2KTo determine an appropriate memory limit for the \u001b[1;36;40mreport-worker\u001b[0m pod, we need to account for the      \r\r\nmemory-intensive nature of its command (\u001b[1;36;40mdd if=/dev/zero of=/dev/null bs=100M count=1\u001b[0m) and provide a \r\r\nbuffer to prevent further OOMKilled events.                                                         \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1;35mBasis for Recommendation\u001b[0m                                                                            \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[36m 1 \u001b[0m\u001b[1mCommand Behavior\u001b[0m:                                                                                \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mThe \u001b[1;36;40mdd\u001b[0m command with \u001b[1;36;40mbs=100M count=1\u001b[0m processes 100Mi of data in a single operation. This       \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m   \u001b[0msuggests the pod needs at least 100Mi of memory for the operation itself.                     \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mAdditional memory is required for the container runtime overhead and other system processes.  \r\r\n\u001b[36m 2 \u001b[0m\u001b[1mCurrent Limit\u001b[0m:                                                                                   \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mThe current memory limit is 64Mi, which is insufficient for the workload.                     \r\r\n\u001b[36m 3 \u001b[0m\u001b[1mBuffer for Stability\u001b[0m:                                                                            \r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mTo ensure stability and avoid future OOMKilled events, a buffer of 50–100% above the estimated\r\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mworkload memory usage is recommended.                                                         \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1;35mSuggested Memory Limit\u001b[0m                                                                              \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1mLimit\u001b[0m: 256Mi                                                                                     \r\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1mRequest\u001b[0m: 128Mi                                                                                   \r\r\n\r\r\nThis configuration provides ample room for the workload and runtime overhead while maintaining      \r\r\nefficient resource usage.                                                                           \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1;35mNext Steps\u001b[0m                                                                                          \r\r\n\r\r\nWould you like me to prepare and apply a patch to update the memory limits for the \u001b[1;36;40mreport-worker\u001b[0m    \r\r\ndeployment?                                                                                         \r\r\n\u001b[?25h"]
